1
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:31,969
[SPEAKER_00]: A question that comes up, or that I see a lot, is how to deal with hateful people.

2
00:00:32,049 --> 00:00:33,590
[SPEAKER_00]: Metta doesn't seem to work.

3
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:33,990
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

4
00:00:40,855 --> 00:00:59,221
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, as we said in other talks, the first thing you do, well, the first thing you have to do, when you're experiencing hate towards somebody, like, I mean, somebody might be hateful to you, but you are experiencing aversion towards that experience.

5
00:01:00,001 --> 00:01:04,683
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't want people to be hateful, because then, you end up being averse and hateful.

6
00:01:05,856 --> 00:01:12,358
[SPEAKER_01]: Or same, if you're experiencing lust and greed, the first thing you have to do is not act out of it.

7
00:01:13,839 --> 00:01:20,841
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if somebody is hateful towards you, you should not be hateful towards them, by body, by speech.

8
00:01:22,401 --> 00:01:33,605
[SPEAKER_01]: Mentally, you might not be able to help yourself to have bad thoughts and so on, but only after you have been accomplished sufficiently enough in non-acting out of hate,

9
00:01:34,757 --> 00:01:43,843
[SPEAKER_01]: Regardless of what hate comes your way, not speaking out of hate, regardless of what hate comes your way, then you will be able to do something about on the level of your mind.

10
00:01:44,384 --> 00:01:47,866
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the problem, the reason why metta doesn't work is because, well, it doesn't work on that level.

11
00:01:48,487 --> 00:01:59,935
[SPEAKER_01]: People would think, oh, I'm experiencing hate, I'm full of aversion, let me do metta, but they do it so to get rid of the aversion, to get rid of the experience that's unpleasant.

12
00:01:59,975 --> 00:02:02,897
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all they want to do metta for is because it's unpleasant otherwise.

13
00:02:04,402 --> 00:02:08,545
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... and acting out of displeasure, that's why you're still averse.

14
00:02:09,967 --> 00:02:18,073
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you you keep acting when things are... you keep trying to get rid of the displeasure, because you're averse to it, that's why you perpetuate your attitude of aversion.

15
00:02:19,945 --> 00:02:36,402
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why the Buddha would often say the words abuse of others, insults and so on, needs to be endured like you would endure heat, cold, bad weather and so on, wind.

16
00:02:36,542 --> 00:02:40,306
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't, you know, like when it's cold, you don't get angry with the winter.

17
00:02:41,607 --> 00:02:43,069
[SPEAKER_01]: You just bear the discomfort.

18
00:02:44,507 --> 00:02:48,248
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure, you get warmer, but you're not full of aversion.

19
00:02:48,308 --> 00:02:49,849
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I hate this discomfort.

20
00:02:50,489 --> 00:02:51,249
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you can't really...

21
00:02:51,449 --> 00:02:55,250
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, you can try, but it's futile, because you know you can't do much about it.

22
00:02:55,831 --> 00:02:57,191
[SPEAKER_01]: So you just try to avoid cold.

23
00:02:57,251 --> 00:02:58,792
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, try and avoid hateful people.

24
00:02:59,972 --> 00:03:01,773
[SPEAKER_01]: But don't try to get rid of the discomfort.

25
00:03:03,853 --> 00:03:05,254
[SPEAKER_01]: In the sense of, um...

26
00:03:05,874 --> 00:03:09,795
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm averse to this, so I'll do everything in my power to not experience this.

27
00:03:10,255 --> 00:03:10,375
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

28
00:03:10,495 --> 00:03:12,516
[SPEAKER_01]: When it arises, you have to endure it.

29
00:03:13,644 --> 00:03:16,925
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what would be the endurance in terms of somebody being hateful to you?

30
00:03:17,065 --> 00:03:18,346
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, not acting back.

31
00:03:18,466 --> 00:03:19,626
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the endurance part.

32
00:03:20,347 --> 00:03:21,627
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the metta part.

33
00:03:21,787 --> 00:03:24,168
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's the prerequisite for metta.

34
00:03:24,448 --> 00:03:42,235
[SPEAKER_01]: If you have sufficiently not acted out of your aversion, out of your lust towards the world, if you have sufficiently withdrawn yourself away from the world through that... through avoiding that unwholesome basis for your action, then, yeah, you're left with just a recognition of your own aversion,

35
00:03:43,553 --> 00:03:50,679
[SPEAKER_01]: In regard to this body experiencing heat, cold, bad weather, abuse of others, others are irrelevant.

36
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:53,722
[SPEAKER_01]: What's relevant is that you don't want to bear it here.

37
00:03:55,804 --> 00:04:04,912
[SPEAKER_01]: Because a number of times, like you can even see that even without matter, when you were in a good mood and somebody hateful, but the hate doesn't reach you, because you remain impetuous, you don't move.

38
00:04:06,426 --> 00:04:08,488
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's like, ah, so really that's the root of the problem.

39
00:04:08,608 --> 00:04:11,410
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't stop the world from being hateful, if they want.

40
00:04:11,470 --> 00:04:13,612
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just, you know, how can you control that?

41
00:04:14,333 --> 00:04:17,055
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can certainly stop yourself from being affected by that.

42
00:04:17,455 --> 00:04:19,377
[SPEAKER_01]: But the first thing to do is stop acting out of it.

43
00:04:19,417 --> 00:04:26,503
[SPEAKER_01]: Stop, stop, you know, doing stuff in return, including, I must do metta, I must do metta, I must do metta, because I can't bear this.

44
00:04:26,543 --> 00:04:27,564
[SPEAKER_01]: No, first you have to bear it.

45
00:04:28,350 --> 00:04:32,412
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what means being accomplished in virtue and restraint.

46
00:04:33,093 --> 00:04:38,576
[SPEAKER_01]: Means knowing that you can bear it even if you don't do anything about it, even if you can't do anything about it.

47
00:04:38,716 --> 00:04:39,456
[SPEAKER_01]: You know for sure.

48
00:04:39,556 --> 00:04:41,478
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, at least I know I can bear it, because I've bared it.

49
00:04:42,778 --> 00:04:48,382
[SPEAKER_01]: And then the mind will start to calm down, and then the things become clear in a sense of, ah, I'm not actually averse towards you.

50
00:04:49,522 --> 00:04:55,826
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm averse towards this body experiencing discomfort of elements and hateful speech from external, sort of, points of view.

51
00:04:57,344 --> 00:04:59,306
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's where the matter begins.

52
00:04:59,946 --> 00:05:00,787
[SPEAKER_01]: Self-aversion.

53
00:05:01,788 --> 00:05:07,192
[SPEAKER_01]: Aversion towards the senses, towards non-control, towards discomfort that comes through them.

54
00:05:08,653 --> 00:05:10,715
[SPEAKER_01]: And mind-friendliness, as we spoke before.

55
00:05:11,456 --> 00:05:20,103
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, even if you're absolutely violently hateful, I'm not abandoning that gateway where the problem would arise for me, from that hate.

56
00:05:20,243 --> 00:05:21,564
[SPEAKER_01]: My problem is not that you're hateful,

57
00:05:22,130 --> 00:05:30,857
[SPEAKER_01]: My problem is if I try to get rid of this body experiencing that hate, but the only reason I would be trying to get rid of that is if I'm still cultivating aversion towards it.

58
00:05:31,498 --> 00:05:35,661
[SPEAKER_01]: But now I'm cultivating the mind of friendliness and benevolence, regardless of what comes this way.

59
00:05:36,421 --> 00:05:37,642
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I cannot be averse.

60
00:05:37,703 --> 00:05:48,671
[SPEAKER_01]: So, no matter how much you shout and you're abusive, the body remains... well, I remain unaverse towards my own senses, towards my own body, that are experiencing all of that hate and elements and so on.

61
00:05:50,347 --> 00:05:52,348
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the root that you deal with.

62
00:05:52,388 --> 00:05:53,509
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the framework, exactly.

63
00:05:54,490 --> 00:05:58,952
[SPEAKER_01]: You maintain, you protect your mind, like a mother protects her only child, as Mathesutra says.

64
00:05:59,433 --> 00:06:05,576
[SPEAKER_01]: You protect your mind on that level, like your precious child, protect the mind of friendliness just there, nothing else will be a problem.

65
00:06:06,297 --> 00:06:10,479
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter how hateful and intense things around get.

66
00:06:10,819 --> 00:06:12,040
[SPEAKER_01]: Mind of friendliness first.

67
00:06:13,368 --> 00:06:15,890
[SPEAKER_01]: And that is truly unlimited state.

68
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:20,573
[SPEAKER_01]: It would be boundless, because it's not bound anymore with perceptions of self or others for that matter.

69
00:06:22,074 --> 00:06:29,599
[SPEAKER_01]: Imagine when... and then you develop confidence on the point of highway robbers, as the suttas say, can come and start violently attacking you with machetes.

70
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:32,281
[SPEAKER_01]: And your mind of friendliness will still not change.

71
00:06:32,841 --> 00:06:33,662
[SPEAKER_01]: And you know that.

72
00:06:34,676 --> 00:06:35,798
[SPEAKER_01]: It's fearlessness as well.

73
00:06:36,018 --> 00:06:36,939
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter what happens.

74
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:39,723
[SPEAKER_01]: Mindfulness cannot be affected.

75
00:06:40,324 --> 00:06:41,746
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why it's a Brahma-vihāra.

76
00:06:41,766 --> 00:06:46,432
[SPEAKER_01]: They would have said, somebody cultivates their mind on that level, rebirth in Brahma realm is guaranteed.

77
00:06:46,973 --> 00:06:49,797
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's just so elevated, so boundless, immeasurable.

78
00:06:51,118 --> 00:07:06,603
[SPEAKER_01]: Above the gratuitous diversification of me, you, mine, all that's been perpetuated, not because of some intellectual error,

79
00:07:07,023 --> 00:07:08,705
[SPEAKER_01]: Not developed in regard to your own body.

80
00:07:08,725 --> 00:07:09,765
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you act.

81
00:07:09,785 --> 00:07:11,867
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you try to get rid of it.

82
00:07:11,887 --> 00:07:14,029
[SPEAKER_01]: So, patience, endurance, as we say so often,

83
00:07:36,343 --> 00:07:43,825
[SPEAKER_01]: Accomplished in virtue, sense-restrained, whatever practice of meditation you do, or contemplation, this is a non-negotiable basis.

84
00:07:44,686 --> 00:07:51,788
[SPEAKER_01]: Accomplished in virtue, having, like as I said, know, you develop a knowledge that I can endure.

85
00:07:52,528 --> 00:07:59,612
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if I can't do anything about it, even if I don't know the way out, I can't figure it out, things are all clouded, I don't understand anything, but used to be.

86
00:07:59,632 --> 00:08:05,956
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it doesn't matter how much doubt you know, but I can endure, because I endured it, and I still am enduring it.

87
00:08:06,897 --> 00:08:08,397
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's accomplished in virtue.

88
00:08:08,838 --> 00:08:14,821
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, when thing passes, which you will have to, you realize, even in that instance, I didn't act.

89
00:08:15,121 --> 00:08:17,583
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even more confidence on account of your virtue grows.

90
00:08:18,003 --> 00:08:26,050
[SPEAKER_01]: Even more gladness then comes, because now you know that even harder circumstances, you still did not act out of that pressure.

91
00:08:26,991 --> 00:08:28,392
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why sīla first.

92
00:08:28,492 --> 00:08:29,613
[SPEAKER_01]: Samādhi comes out of it.

93
00:08:30,153 --> 00:08:33,236
[SPEAKER_01]: Immovability of your mind will come out of the confidence of sīla.

94
00:08:33,776 --> 00:08:37,039
[SPEAKER_01]: That's exactly what the Buddha describes in so many ways, so many times.

95
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:41,803
[SPEAKER_00]: Realizing that there is no boundary then.

96
00:08:42,622 --> 00:08:43,603
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, sure, sure.

97
00:08:43,723 --> 00:08:46,365
[SPEAKER_01]: But I don't want to get into describing what's after.

98
00:08:47,125 --> 00:08:55,131
[SPEAKER_01]: It will become self-evident what's after if you become accomplished in virtue and stop acting out of aversion, out of agreeable and disagreeable.

99
00:08:55,731 --> 00:08:56,092
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

100
00:08:56,432 --> 00:08:56,772
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

101
00:08:56,972 --> 00:09:04,878
[SPEAKER_01]: Cultivate... Don't think that cultivation of that endurance, accomplishment in virtue is somehow irrelevant.

102
00:09:05,038 --> 00:09:06,039
[SPEAKER_01]: That is the practice.

103
00:09:06,099 --> 00:09:08,701
[SPEAKER_01]: Samādhi is within that and pañña is within that.

104
00:09:09,401 --> 00:09:10,082
[SPEAKER_01]: Not after that.

105
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:15,190
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you're accomplishing virtue, you already have a basis that contains samādhi and pañña.

106
00:09:18,193 --> 00:09:19,675
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you never abandon that.

107
00:09:19,915 --> 00:09:21,216
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, I don't...

108
00:09:21,236 --> 00:09:23,299
[SPEAKER_01]: I will not act out of the pressure of the senses.

109
00:09:25,902 --> 00:09:27,764
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if I can't figure it out, I will not act.

110
00:09:28,124 --> 00:09:28,805
[SPEAKER_01]: I will sustain it.

111
00:09:29,305 --> 00:09:30,367
[SPEAKER_01]: And that will accomplish you.

112
00:09:31,608 --> 00:09:32,088
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's it.

